WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Shogi Club

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Urushi Yaotome

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Ayumu Tanaka

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Takeru Kakuryu

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Rin Kagawa

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.080
Senpai.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.290
If you have time, would you like
to get together over Golden Week?

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.420
G-get together?

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.250
Is he asking me...

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.380
To go out on a date!?

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.080
On the last day.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.250
If you don't have any other plans, that is.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.500
No, wait! How can he ask me this?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.330
Rin-chan is right over there.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.580
...And Rin-chan doesn't seem to mind at all.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.290
What is happening?

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.130
Is this kind of thing normal in athletic clubs?

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.130
In that case, I can't freak out about this.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.250
I have to show them that I am a calm, composed senpai.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:43.630
Senpai?

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.710
I-I'm free on the last day.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.630
I don't have plans.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.250
Thank you very much!

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.080
I'm so glad you said yes! I can't wait!

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.630
Then is one o'clock a good time to meet up?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.830
That's about the time I was thinking.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.170
Do you think Kakuryu-san would join us?

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.040
Probably.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.830
Then let's invite him!

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.290
Good idea.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:16.000
We don't get vacations very often, so we were really
hoping we could all do something fun together.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:23.080
Of course. We're getting together "as a club."

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.040
Today is         Books are due back

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.040
April 28 (Thur.)

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.040
May 9 (Mon.)

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:30.080
Looks like the shogi club is planning to do something.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.040
Last day of Golden Week.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.000
You wanna go, Sakurako?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:34.830
No.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:36.670
Oh, okay.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.710
The Fable

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:39.500
Another day...

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.330
A different day during Golden Week...

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.250
I want you to be with me.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:54.630
Now, let's take one step forward

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:58.040
Let me feel your heartbeat

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.290
Tactics require a poker face

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:06.380
Because I don't want my opponent to realize

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.830
For distance, a few centimeters

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.960
Take the long way

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.500
Aiming for a smile

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.880
A secret strategy

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:23.040
An airtight defense

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.250
Just a little more

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.710
I'll meet you halfway, so look the other way

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.710
I get scared of being hurt

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.920
There are nights like that

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.420
A chance that comes from crossed signals

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:47.710
I won't let it escape me. I'll turn the tables

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.420
Now, let's take one step forward

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:56.580
Write your own story

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:03.170
The opening sentence always starts with "actually," "I always"

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.710
The twist is in progressive tense

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:10.080
Let me feel your heartbeat

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:13.540
Tactics require a poker face

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:18.790
Because I don't want my opponent to realize

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:26.330
Game 9: I Want to Make Memories, Senpai

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.920
Whoa, I found one!

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.130
No, I didn't.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.330
It turns out they're actually pretty hard to find, huh?

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.670
She said she wanted me to be with her...

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:44.830
So I kind of got my hopes up.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.920
You said you wanted it for a bookmark?

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:48.710
Uh-huh.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.000
And you can't use a three-leafed one?

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.420
They're practically the same.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.040
They're completely different.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.000
Four-leafed clovers bring good luck.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:01.880
I don't really believe in all that superstitious stuff.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.040
You just don't understand the heart
of a dreamer, Takeru-kun.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:11.420
But hey, if you say that's what you want,
Sakurako, I'll find one if it's the last thing I do.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:13.330
Uh-huh.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.380
Thank you.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:23.330
Please, it's no big deal.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.500
Not just for that.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.960
For always hanging out with me.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:32.580
You know I'm really shy, and I don't have a lot of friends.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.040
So it makes me really happy to have you.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.250
So Takeru-kun...

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.380
If it's okay with you, I hope we can be friends forever.

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:57.540
Yeah. I'll be your friend until you say
you don't like it anymore.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:58.460
Yeah.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:03.880
I found one.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.130
I found a four-leafed clover!

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:08.080
Really!?

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.000
See? How do you like that!?

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.380
I'm sorry! Are you okay!?

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.790
I can't believe you fell.

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:37.750
That's what you get for not believing
in lucky four-leafed clovers.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:40.960
No...

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.880
That was super ultra lucky.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.500
I hope it makes a good bookmark.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:59.080
Yeah!

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:16.330
Takeru-kun.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:18.670
Hm? What's up?

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:31.630
Oh right. You're not athletic like me.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.170
Get plenty of rest when you get home, okay?

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.080
Yeah.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:51.130
This is not good, Tanaka-san.
If we don't hurry, we'll be late.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:52.420
Let's run.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:00.750
No. I wouldn't want to trouble Senpai
by showing up covered in sweat.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.170
Pardon me.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.330
Urushi!

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.330
What are you doing in this neck of the woods?

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.250
Oh, you know...

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.250
What about you?

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:26.920
We're doing this!

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.380
Sweets Endurance Race

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.380
Collect ten stamps to win your choice of free cake!

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.290
Sweets endurance race?

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:33.540
You eat dessert, get a stamp, eat, get a stamp...

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.460
Until you make it to the finish line!

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.250
What in the heck?

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:39.080
What indeed?

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:41.960
But why would you...

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.500
Because the sweets are there!

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:48.670
Anyway, we're going to eat all the sweets
in town before Golden Week is out!

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.000
Aren't we!

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.080
And this is the first stop!

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.080
Care to join us, Urushi?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.750
Today isn't... really...

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.670
Er, I mean...

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:04.830
You're on a date!

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:05.750
I am not!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:09.290
That's why you were checking out
your reflection in the window!

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.130
How long were you watching me!?

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:15.290
I told you, I'm not!

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.790
I thought it was a date, but then it wasn't!

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.790
He was asking me if I wanted to
get together with the whole shogi club!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:34.040
I'm sorry it turned out not to be a date.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.460
I'm not upset about it...

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.960
I was just a little disappointed.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.330
Senpai!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.000
Sorry to keep you waiting, Senpai.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.130
Okay, but why are you speedwalking?

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:07.000
Is that... for the Sweets Endurance Race?

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.710
Oh! You've heard of it?

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:09.500
I have!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:10.830
Sweets Endurance Race

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:12.920
I'm on my second run-through!

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:16.080
Well...

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.500
We can't let her beat us!

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.330
Come on, let the race begin!

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.040
See you later, Rin-chan, Ayumu-kun!

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.880
Don't worry, Urushi. You look very cute.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.790
Wh-why would Maki say that?

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.250
You are very cute, Senpai.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:38.580
Stop that.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.830
Hey, Ayumu, you're late!

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:54.920
Okay, let's give this a shot.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.420
You set a new record.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:11.750
Wow.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.170
Wait, is it wow-worthy?

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.080
I've never done this before, so I don't know.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:18.880
Would you like to try it?

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:22.250
Okay, sure.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.250
Uh, umm...

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:29.920
You can do it, Ms. President!

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:49.750
You set a new record, too.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.460
Even your records are cute, Senpai.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.420
I told you to stop that.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.250
So cute.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.830
Behold my magnificent jumping powers!

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.330
You call that a jump?

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.960
Take that! Full combo ba-dum-bum!

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.250
You won't beat me!

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.670
Behold my magnificent cadence!

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.540
Man, you kids are full of energy.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.330
That's former athletes for you.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.540
Charge!

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.540
Pawn

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.540
Wars

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.170
Wh-what is this?

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.750
They turned shogi pawns into fighter planes!

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:50.830
That's an awfully niche game...

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:52.040
Let's play it, Ayumu!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.130
Yes, Senpai!

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.210
We can do this, Senpai.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.380
Go get 'em, Ms. President!

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:02.040
They're coming from the right!

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:03.420
You got this!

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.170
Look out!

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:08.670
You're doing great, Senpai.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.210
It's huge!

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.130
Alright! They won't beat us!

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.420
Well done!

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.540
Senpai, you did it!

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:28.250
Amazing!

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:28.790
I knew you could do it!

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.710
I used up too much energy.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:38.540
But we won.

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:39.380
Yeah.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.130
Okay!

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:44.130
That was a pretty good warmup.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.920
Are you ready for the main event?

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:53.000
I call it...

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.040
Air Hockey Doubles...

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.580
Golden Week Cup!

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.130
We can do it, Senpai!

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.080
Yeah!

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.500
Nice shot, Kakuryu-san!

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:11.210
Loser pays the price. They buy everybody a soda.

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:13.710
Sorry about that, Ayumu.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:16.420
That's alright. We can turn this around!

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:17.130
Yeah.

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:20.750
Next time... I'm making that shot!

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:37.750
Senpai.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.170
I have a plan.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.500
Oh, come on...

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.170
What do you guys think you're doing?

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:47.170
I'll block with both hands.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.920
You focus on offense, Senpai.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.790
Like it's so easy to use both hands.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:54.210
Amateur thinking.

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.540
Uh, forget about if this plan can work.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:00.130
More importantly, he's so close, it's embarrassing!

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:02.130
Is something the matter?

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:03.630
What do you think!?

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:06.290
We're gonna turn this around in one fell swoop!

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:08.540
Yeah...

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.380
Wow. He really is stopping every shot, all by himself.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:45.130
This feels like I've been put in a compromising position...

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.250
What are you guys doing!?

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.630
Senpai! Now's our chance!

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:19.960
I'm so sorry. You're getting punished, and it's all my fault.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:24.630
It's okay. I was happy to be on
the same team as you, so I don't mind.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:29.000
There he goes embarrassing me again...

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:32.540
It's too bad we missed that last shot.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.750
Oh, that? Yeah.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:41.710
But we wouldn't have even had
a chance without your defense.

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:44.670
Looks like I owe you again, Ayumu.

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:48.000
You don't owe me. I did it because I wanted to.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:53.830
I know. But if there's anything I can do for you,
make sure to tell me, okay?

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:55.330
Thank you, Senpai.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:57.790
Okay! Well, let's go back.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:58.630
Okay.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:01.670
Senpai!

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:04.960
It's not too soon to take you up on your offer, is it?

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.210
Oh! You thought of something? What?

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.750
They're taking forever.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:15.960
They really are.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:19.210
Kakuryu-san! Please excuse me!

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.500
What the?

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.500
Koalas Macho

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:28.880
Koalas Macho

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:28.880
Chocolate

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:28.880
Koalas Macho?

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:30.790
They're so good!

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.380
And these boxes are so big!

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.290
Find me!

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.290
Super Swole Macho Koala

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.790
Super Swole Macho Koala?

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:47.380
Some rare Koalas Macho boxes have a Super Swole
Macho Koala that's supposed to bring good luck!

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:52.250
Good luck...

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:57.000
Maybe I'll try to get a box, too.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:58.460
Got nothing else to do.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:04.580
You want to take pictures together?
And that's really the favor you're going to ask for?

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:05.460
Yes.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:07.830
I want pictures with both of us.

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:10.460
Uh, okay.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:14.580
What? Are you nervous?

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.830
Yes. I've never done this before.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:19.420
Well, then you don't have to be nervous.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:22.920
I've done this a few times, so you can just leave it to me!

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.420
Okay. It's gonna take the first pic.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:29.580
R-right!

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:33.880
Heh heh. First pic and I'm already
making the promoted pawn sign!

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:37.580
Ack, it's backwards!

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:39.080
Y-yes it is.

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:43.130
Darn it, I messed up! Can he tell I'm nervous, too?

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:44.630
Senpai.

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:45.710
Wh-what?

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.210
Thank you for that.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.460
I'm a little less nervous now.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.380
That's exactly what I was going for!

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:56.040
Always on point, Senpai!

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:57.630
Next! Time for the second one!

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.000
That's scary!

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.080
Is that us as aliens?

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.790
No filters! None!

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:06.500
You know...

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:08.630
This is starting to be fun!

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:09.920
I agree!

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:15.130
But wow, you really do always have
the exact same look on your face.

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:18.710
The next one's the last one, so let's finish it
off with the promoted pawn pose!

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.290
Alright.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.080
You're blinking, Ayumu! And it's the last picture!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:32.420
Come on, Senpai, your eyes are closed, too!

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:35.290
And your promoted pawn sign is backwards again.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.000
Both of ours are.

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:43.330
Huh?

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:47.250
I can't believe we had one picture left.

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:49.330
We let our guard down.

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:51.630
But thank you for doing that.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:53.960
I'm glad I got to take pictures with you.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:57.000
Really... Well, good.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:00.000
I had fun, too.

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.670
And I got to see something special.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.540
Koalas Macho

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.540
Chocolate

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.710
Wh-what happened here?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.670
Golden Week is the best!

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:19.830
It is fun, isn't it?

00:19:20.710 --> 00:19:21.460
Yeah!

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.790
Alright, now I'm pumped!

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:28.750
Air Hockey Doubles: Golden Week Cup
Round Two! Let's go!

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:30.790
Bring it on!

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:33.580
We're still doing that?

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:58.420
The term "next to" is surprisingly versatile

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:05.380
For example, you can be one meter apart
from someone and still be "next to" them

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:13.420
We're in a stale-mate, in a town dyed rosy red

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:22.330
I want to know your real feelings, but you evade and keep walking

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:31.960
Then I realize we're within 50 centimeters (doo-wop x2)

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:39.630
Or am I outside of 50 centimeters? (doo-wop x2)

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:47.080
What is the reason we walk home together? (doo-wop x2)

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:51.290
Unable to ask, our shadows align

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.420
Excuse me, Mikage-san?

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.540
Uh, umm...

00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:29.500
You can have it.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.330
I just happened to get one, by coincidence.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:37.960
It's supposed to be good luck.

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:40.580
What if I get lucky again?

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.330
Takeru-kun.

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:48.170
What?

00:21:48.420 --> 00:21:50.420
A boy just told me he likes me.

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.540
He asked me to go out with him.

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:57.500
Wow. So did you give him an answer?

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.000
No, not yet.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.210
How could this happen!?

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:06.170
What if, on a whim, Sakurako decides
to go out with this guy!?

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.380
Lucky, my ass!

00:22:09.790 --> 00:22:14.420
But wait... A decent man would want
the woman he loves to be happy...

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:18.380
I don't really understand...

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:21.080
What it means to "like" someone.

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:26.830
What does it feel like to like someone?

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:29.380
H-how should I know?

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:39.210
I think... It feels like, it's fun to be with them,
and you want to do things for them...

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:47.420
You want to see them happy, and suddenly
you realize you're always thinking about them.

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.750
And... I guess...

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:56.630
Maybe it's about whether or not your heart
starts beating faster when you're with them.

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:02.670
I see...

00:23:03.460 --> 00:23:05.210
It makes sense now.

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:13.080
That's enough, right? This is embarrassing.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:14.250
Yeah.

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:19.170
So... I decided... I'm going to turn that boy down.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:20.790
Really.

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:22.460
Because I realized.

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:23.580
Realized what?

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:26.130
Takeru-kun.

00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:30.290
I like...

00:23:30.670 --> 00:23:32.630
That you taught me about liking someone. Thank you.

00:23:36.170 --> 00:23:36.960
Sure.

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:47.630
Sakurako, you're looking kind of flushed.

00:23:47.630 --> 00:23:49.040
Do you have a fever?

00:23:49.460 --> 00:23:52.000
No, I think I'm okay.

00:23:52.420 --> 00:23:53.540
Are you sure?

00:23:58.710 --> 00:24:00.710
I'm sharing the luck.

00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:09.380
Takeru-kun?

00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:11.540
It's nothing, I'm fine!
